---
import BookLayout from "../../layouts/BookLayout.astro";
import StatusMarker from "../../components/StatusMarker.astro";
import book from "../../data/book.json";
import { groupBookRows, loadBookRows } from "../../lib/book-status";
import { orangeRevision } from "../../data/orange-sources";
const bookGroups = groupBookRows(loadBookRows(book.chapters));
---

<BookLayout>
  <div class="book-introduction">
    <img src="/projects/orange/book-cover.svg" alt="The Orange Book cover: the Orange emblem in cream on an orange field." width="1600" height="2400" />
    <div>
      <p>This site hosts two drafts. Neither is a finished book.</p>
      <p>The pages here are the earlier manuscript, <a href={book.sourceUrl}>docs/THE_ORANGE_BOOK.md</a>: the original 17-chapter text plus appendices. It is an earlier draft. Chapter numbers stay as they are until one renumbering pass later. This is not the Novice, Journeyman, and Master curriculum.</p>
      <p class="book-introduction-note">That curriculum is a separate work in docs/book/, being written now. It is not these pages, and it is not complete. These pages are also not a normative specification, proof, assurance report, license grant, or release claim.</p>
      <span class="book-edition">Living pre-alpha reader guide</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Novice, Journeyman, and Master</h2>
  <p>That name belongs to the curriculum in docs/book/. This site does not list its chapters. It is being written now, and it is not finished.</p>

  <section class="book-checks" aria-labelledby="book-checks-title">
    <h2 id="book-checks-title">How the hosted chapters are checked</h2>
    <p>The hosted chapters are manuscript {book.version}, snapshot {book.snapshot}, revision {book.revision}. The site checks that text against the vendored manuscript. That check is not a new compiler run. The home-page listing is compiler/fixtures/s3b/valid-sha256-functions.or. compiler/crates/orangec/tests/s3b_conformance.rs expects sha256::round0_a = 0x5d6aebcd. A fixture result is not a proof or a security claim. Compiler sentences on this site were checked against orange main {orangeRevision} on 9 October 2026, a later revision than this manuscript. Compiler tests were not re-run.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="book-start">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/book/preface/">Start the manuscript <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </p>

  <section id="book-parts" class="book-contents-list" aria-labelledby="book-contents-title">
    <h2 id="book-contents-title">Inside the earlier manuscript</h2>
    {bookGroups.map((group) => (
      <div class="book-contents-group">
        {group.part && <h3>{group.part}</h3>}
        <ol>
          {group.rows.map((row) => (
            <li data-status={row.status}>
              {row.href ? (
                <a href={row.href}>
                  <span>{row.title}</span>
                  <StatusMarker status={row.status} />
                </a>
              ) : (
                <span>
                  <span>{row.title}</span>
                  <StatusMarker status={row.status} />
                </span>
              )}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>
</BookLayout>
